Small follow-up fix on branch `feature/SFCC-236_product-card-shared-component` in `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa`. A just-approved, already-made fix changed `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmSlideIndicator/zimmSlideIndicator.css.ts`'s `isActive: true` branch from `var(--zimm-color-border-focus)` to `var(--zimm-color-bg-05)` — a category correction (a `background:` CSS property should use a `background.*`-derived token, not a `border.*` one), not a value change: `border.focus` and `background['05']` both resolve to the identical hex (`grey[900]`) in `theme/foundation/colour.ts`, confirmed already. Nothing renders differently.

This broke `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmSlideIndicator/zimmSlideIndicator.css.test.ts`, which still hard-asserts the old value and was never updated. Read the file first — it currently has:

```ts
test('active segment uses border-focus, not the previously-wired (visually-identical but semantically wrong) bg-05', () => {
  const { dot } = ZimmSlideIndicator.baseStyle({ isActive: true });
  expect(dot.background).toBe('var(--zimm-color-border-focus)');
});
```

Update this test to match the corrected implementation — flip both the assertion and the test's own name/framing, since the old name asserts the *opposite* conclusion from what's now true:

```ts
test('active segment uses bg-05, the category-correct token for a background property — border-focus and bg-05 share the identical confirmed value (grey[900]), this only corrects which named token expresses it', () => {
  const { dot } = ZimmSlideIndicator.baseStyle({ isActive: true });
  expect(dot.background).toBe('var(--zimm-color-bg-05)');
});
```
(Use that exact wording unless you find the surrounding file's convention suggests a better phrasing — use your judgement on wording, but the assertion value must be `'var(--zimm-color-bg-05)'`.)

**Do not touch** the `inactive segment uses border-secondary...` test right below it — that branch was correctly left unchanged by the prior fix (no `background.*` counterpart exists for `border.secondary`, a genuine foundation gap, not something to fix here).

Also check the file's top-level docblock (lines 4-9) — it currently frames itself as confirming "the two colour tokens" (implying `border-focus`/`border-secondary`) against Figma. Add a short note (don't delete the existing Figma-confirmation provenance, it's still valid evidence for the *value*) clarifying that a later pass corrected the *active* segment's token from `border-focus` to the category-correct `bg-05` — same confirmed value, different token name. Follow this codebase's own established pattern for documenting a "was X, corrected to Y, here's why" history (e.g. `zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts`'s badge-height comment does this) rather than silently rewriting the docblock as if `bg-05` was always the answer.

When done, run just this test file and report pass/fail, and confirm `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean. Do not stage, do not commit.

